David","also":"","summary":"Beloved, the eighth and youngest son of Jesse, a citizen of Bethlehem. His father seems to have been a man in humble life. His mother’s name is not recorded.","verses":896,"father":"Jesse","mother":"","v":[1,3,5,7]},{"id":"solomon_2762","name":"Solomon","also":"Jedidiah","summary":"Peaceful, (Heb. Shelomoh), David’s second son by Bathsheba, i.e., the first after their legal marriage (2 Sam. 12). He was probably born about B.C. 1035 (1 Chr. 22:5; 29:1).","verses":273,"father":"David","mother":"Bathsheba","v":[1,2,7,8,10,11,12,13,15,16,18]},{"id":"hiram_1532","name":"Hiram","also":"Huram","summary":"Also “Huram” and “Horam,” king of Tyre. He entered into an alliance with David, and assisted him in building his palace by sending him able workmen, and also cedar-trees and fir-trees from Lebanon (2 Sam. 5:11; 1 Chr. 14:1).","verses":23,"father":"Huram","mother":"","v":[1,2,7,8,10,11,12,18]},{"id":"adoniram_102","name":"Adoniram","also":"Adoram, Hadoram","summary":"One who was “over the tribute;” i.e., “over the levy.” He was stoned by the Israelites after they had revolted from Rehoboam (2 Chr. 10:18).","verses":5,"father":"Abda","mother":"","v":[14]}],"places":[{"id":"tyre_1184","name":"Tyre","kind":"City","lat":33.26807,"lon":35.20936,"summary":"A rock, now es-Sur; an ancient Phoenician city, about 23 miles, in a direct line, north of Acre, and 20 south of Sidon. Sidon was the oldest Phoenician city, but Tyre had a longer and more illustrious history.","verses":52,"v":[1]},{"id":"lebanon_720","name":"Lebanon","kind":"Region","lat":33.92154,"lon":35.89897,"summary":"White, “the white mountain of Syria,” is the loftiest and most celebrated mountain range in Syria. It is a branch running southward from the Caucasus, and at its lower end forking into two parallel ranges, the eastern or Anti-Lebanon, and the western or Lebanon proper.","verses":56,"v":[6,9,14]},{"id":"gebal_449","name":"Gebal","kind":"City","lat":34.1191,"lon":35.64614,"summary":